36 PM PT Nov 10","account":"T2","old":"60–150s, ask 47–58¢, BRTI move ≥2bp, 10-minute trend ≥4bp, $5","new":"60–150s, ask 45–60¢, BRTI move ≥2bp, 10-minute trend ≥3bp, $5","reason":"Zero settled trades after ~9 hours. The 47–58¢ / 4bp-trend cousin almost never lined up live (T’s overlapping fill was 59¢ with a −2.5bp trend, which T2 would reject). Widening the ask to T’s 45–60¢ band and easing the trend floor from 4bp to 3bp is the smallest relaxation that stays clearly profitable on the 18-day first-hit backtest (~19 trades/day, +$58 after fees vs the original 13/day and +$130). The suggested 45–180s + 45–60¢ + 3bp combo backtested negative (−$61) and was not used. Time window and the 2bp BRTI-move threshold are unchanged."},{"time_pt":"6:36 PM PT Nov 10","account":"LFC","old":"A’s late favorite (ask ≥0.80, ≤50s left) + favorite ask continuously >0.55 for 90s + hard stop below 0.50, 5% equity","new":"A’s late favorite (ask ≥0.80) allowed from ≤70s left + favorite ask continuously >0.55 for 60s + hard stop below 0.50, 5% equity","reason":"The 90s confirm was not the main live blocker (0 filter_blocks; two late favorites held ~89s but could not fill into a one-sided late book). Shortening the confirm to 60s eases that filter. Allowing the same ≥0.80 late-favorite price rule from 70s left (instead of 50s) aims to lift an ask before the late book goes one-sided. A 1-minute backtest of slightly earlier late entries stayed strongly positive; a looser 120s-left proxy was still positive but weaker, so the late gate stops at 70s. Hard stop and sizing are unchanged. A’s own 50s late-favorite rule is unchanged."},{"time_pt":"6:36 PM PT Nov 10","account":"M5","old":"T’s 60–150s / 45–60¢ rule, plus 3 consecutive polls where book imbalance I is strictly on the same side (I>0 for UP, I<0 for DOWN), $5","new":"Same T entry rule, plus 2 consecutive polls where I > −0.25 for UP or I < +0.25 for DOWN, $5","reason":"Zero trades in ~26 hours even though T filled three times in that span. On all three of those T fills, top-of-book imbalance I was on the opposite side (or nearly flat), so a strict same-side I>0 / I<0 filter could never agree. Lowered the agreement floor from 0 to −0.25 / +0.25 and required 2 agreeing snapshots instead of 3. That would have allowed 2 of T’s 3 live trades (the UP fill at I=−0.25 would still be blocked). Expected rate approaches T’s when the book is not strongly opposed (T’s 18-day backtest is ~10 trades/day / +$115 at $5; live T has been quieter)."}],"coinbase_lag":{"reachable":true,"samples":900,"last_price":57912.67,"last_diff_bp":-4.5479,"mean_abs_bp":9.9003},"btc_minutes":{"as_of":"11:00:05 PM PT","source":"BRTI","last":57946.1,"series":[{"ts":1795240860,"t":"10:01 PM","c":55711.57,"d":27.5,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795240920,"t":"10:02 PM","c":55711.07,"d":-0.5,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795240980,"t":"10:03 PM","c":55666.82,"d":-44.25,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795241040,"t":"10:04 PM","c":55664.27,"d":-2.55,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795241100,"t":"10:05 PM","c":55718.79,"d":54.52,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795241160,"t":"10:06 PM","c":55703.83,"d":-14.96,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795241220,"t":"10:07 PM","c":55700.16,"d":-3.67,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795241280,"t":"10:08 PM","c":55647.51,"d":-52.65,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795241340,"t":"10:09 PM","c":55702.03,"d":54.52,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795241400,"t":"10:10 PM","c":55672.74,"d":-29.29,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795241460,"t":"10:11 PM","c":55751.04,"d":78.3,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795241520,"t":"10:12 PM","c":55634.33,"d":-116.71,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795241580,"t":"10:13 PM","c":55572.44,"d":-61.89,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795241640,"t":"10:14 PM","c":55642.44,"d":70.0,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795241700,"t":"10:15 PM","c":55550.9,"d":-91.54,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795241760,"t":"10:16 PM","c":55302.86,"d":-248.04,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795241820,"t":"10:17 PM","c":55651.45,"d":348.59,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795241880,"t":"10:18 PM","c":55874.78,"d":223.33,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795241940,"t":"10:19 PM","c":55907.48,"d":32.7,"dir":"up"}